evolution-sieve-filters (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix several data-corruption bugs in the visual/raw editor: a
    ":regex" match type was silently downgraded to ":contains", a value
    list with more than one entry (e.g. ["a", "b"]) was truncated to
    its first element, and a disabled "if false" test was
    re-serialized as "if true", inverting the rule's logic. Any
    construct the editor can't safely represent now falls back to a
    read-only "opaque" copy instead of being silently mangled.
  * Add ":regex" as a supported match type in the visual editor
    (requires the Sieve "regex" extension on the server).
  * Add support for multi-value conditions (a Sieve string list, e.g.
    matching several senders at once): editable as a comma-separated
    field, with "\," / "\\" escaping for a literal comma or backslash
    within a value.
  * Add per-rule enable/disable in the visual editor. A disabled rule
    is saved as "if false # <test>", the same convention used by
    Roundcube's managesieve plugin, so the original test survives
    re-enabling and stays compatible with scripts managed by other
    Sieve tools.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:27:01 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add SASL GSSAPI (Kerberos) authentication support: automatic
    mechanism negotiation now picks GSSAPI when the caller has a usable
    Kerberos ticket (e.g. an Active Directory-joined workstation),
    falling back to SCRAM/PLAIN/etc. otherwise; --mech GSSAPI forces it
    explicitly. New optional build dependency on libkrb5, used only to
    detect a usable ticket for automatic negotiation.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:24:22 +0000

